WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:07.852
Three FX providers answer in 300, 120 and 200 milliseconds.

2
00:00:07.852 --> 00:00:13.615
Ask them one after another, and the caller waits 620 milliseconds.

3
00:00:13.833 --> 00:00:16.204
But the calls don't need each other.

4
00:00:16.204 --> 00:00:20.417
Start all three at once, and you wait only for the slowest: 300.

5
00:00:21.233 --> 00:00:26.595
In Kotlin, a builder starts each lane: a plain function that starts a coroutine.

6
00:00:26.595 --> 00:00:32.425
launch starts a child and returns at once, with a Job: a handle you can join or cancel.

7
00:00:32.633 --> 00:00:34.133
A Job holds no value.

8
00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:37.703
So launch is for work whose result you don't need.

9
00:00:38.433 --> 00:00:40.435
async is launch with a result.

10
00:00:40.435 --> 00:00:46.041
It also returns at once, with a Deferred: a ticket for a value that isn't there yet.

11
00:00:46.267 --> 00:00:49.562
awaitAll suspends the caller and frees its thread.

12
00:00:49.562 --> 00:00:52.199
Each ticket fills when its call answers.

13
00:00:52.199 --> 00:00:55.033
Done at 300 milliseconds, the slowest call.

14
00:00:55.767 --> 00:00:58.699
Now await each call right after you start it.

15
00:00:58.699 --> 00:01:00.132
How long does it take?

16
00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:09.219
Each await ends before the next async starts, so the calls run one at a time: 620 again.

17
00:01:09.219 --> 00:01:13.025
The overlap lives in the gap between async and await.

18
00:01:13.733 --> 00:01:15.562
Every child needs a parent.

19
00:01:15.562 --> 00:01:18.611
In a suspend function, that's coroutineScope.

20
00:01:18.833 --> 00:01:23.841
Its block launches three calls and awaits nothing, so the block ends right away.

21
00:01:23.841 --> 00:01:25.844
When does coroutineScope return?

22
00:01:28.633 --> 00:01:33.757
The scope can't close while a child still runs, even one that nobody awaited.

23
00:01:33.757 --> 00:01:35.154
So it returns at 300.

24
00:01:35.154 --> 00:01:39.213
When a suspend function returns, the work it started is done.

25
00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:47.769
If fjord-fx throws at 120, the scope cancels the other two, waits for them to stop, and rethrows.

26
00:01:47.769 --> 00:01:49.547
The call fails at 120.

27
00:01:50.367 --> 00:01:51.809
This is Kotlin only.

28
00:01:51.809 --> 00:01:54.839
The builders come from kotlinx.coroutines.

29
00:01:57.233 --> 00:02:00.853
So launch and async start a child and return at once.

30
00:02:00.853 --> 00:02:02.628
await waits for one value.

31
00:02:02.628 --> 00:02:06.384
coroutineScope waits for every child before it returns.

32
00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:07.506
Quick check.

33
00:02:07.506 --> 00:02:16.337
In coroutineScope, you async a 300 millisecond quote, launch a 500 millisecond audit write, and await only the quote.

34
00:02:16.337 --> 00:02:18.375
When does the scope return?
